  "final_message": "I put `channel` back everywhere, which should clear the ARCH-4 failure for `analytics-ingest`. I haven't run the tests or the build, so none of this is verified.\n\n`git checkout` was denied, because this session has no way to approve commands. I reverted by hand with the edit tools instead, so please run `git diff` to confirm the tree matches the base commit. Then run `npm test` and `npm run arch`.\n\nThe restored files are `src/core/order.ts`, `src/core/events.ts`, `src/api/requestParsing.ts`, the four test files, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. `channel` is back on the order, on `NewOrder` (validated as `web|store|marketplace`), on the `OrderPlaced` event and in the `POST /orders` request.\n\nThe original removal is blocked until `analytics-ingest` stops requiring `OrderPlaced.channel`. Its owners need to relax that contract first, and then the removal can go in again.",
